\section{Large pulse of 20-inch PMT}
\label{1:testing}

The large signal testing of the PMT was conducted using a self-trigger mode, and the electronic threshold was set to 1000\,ADCs (around 120\,mV) or 4000\,ADCs (around 480\,mV) for fine range. Three electronics channels of the same GCU use the same trigger, which means when any one of them is triggered, the other two channels will synchronously acquire data too. The time window per trigger is set to ten microseconds. Each run includes 10k triggers events. Due to the high trigger threshold, only large pulses generated by the PMT itself originating from natural radioactivity and cosmic rays are recorded\,\cite{zhangyu-large-pulse,Zhang:2023dha}. A survey of large pulse rate versus threshold is shown in Fig.\,\ref{fig:thre_scan}.

