\section{Summary}
\label{1:summary}

With the mass testing of JUNO 20-inch potted PMT with 1F3 electronics prototype at the Pan-Asia testing platform, we get a batch samples on the PMT self generated pulses. The rate is around 100\,Hz per PMT for both MCP or dynode PMTs on the ground with a threshold around 100\,mV (or 10\,P.E.). Besides, the time and charge features of the PMT self generated pulses are evaluated. Thanks to the broad amplitude distribution of the signals, we further investigated the time distribution of the after pulses, as well as the the variation of their number and charge with respect to the main pulse charge. Based on the data from fine range and coarse range, we examined the linearity between amplitude and charge, the timing of both dynamic ranges, and the consistency in amplitude and charge between the two ranges.

