    %
    In this case, the integrality of $f$ insists $\a+\b \in 2\mathbb{Z}$ and whenever $p+\a$ is odd, $p+\b$ is also odd by integrality of $f$, making, $\widetilde{\a}$, $\widetilde{\b}$ simultaneously to be integers, so, $\text{KP}_{\widetilde{\a},\widetilde{\b}}$ interpretation is available if $0\leq \widetilde{\a},\widetilde{\b} \leq 2p$, outside of which range does not give duality. Therefore, to find new duality, we scan the rest cases, $p+\a \in 2\mathbb{Z}$:
