Lieber Wilhelm,

zunaechst allerbeste Gruesse aus Erlangen. Ich hoffe, Dir geht es auch gut. Ich schreibe Dir nun lieber auch in Englisch, falls Du meine Kommentare auch anderen Editoren schicken moechtest.

We hereby would like to submit the attached manuscript on

Local perturbations of banded Toeplitz matrices 

for publication in Inventiones. Let us briefly advertise the achievements. Banded Toeplitz matrices appear in many applications and there are many works on half-sided restrictions which are of index-theoretic nature (see the books in the references). As to finite size restrictions, there exists only a very limited literature. The main contribution is from Harold Widom from 1974. While deep and inspiring, that work is very complicated and the main results need hypothesis that are in practice very hard to check. Moreover, it does not produce formulas for the limit spectra that are very trackable (for numerics, e.g.). In an earlier work, we rederived and extended Widom's results by transfer matrix methods. The submitted work goes much further. It deals with local perturbations of Toeplitz matrices and shows surprising spectral theoretic results that allow to interpolate between cyclic and truncated Toeplitz matrices. Furthermore, by using techniques from algebraic geometry it is shown that the Widom-type assumptions hold for a set of Toeplitz matrices of full measure. All results are illustrated by numerics.

We would not have submitted this draft to such a prestigious journal if we would not have been convinced that this work constitutes a considerable advance, both on the level of results and techniques.

Best regards

Hermann Schulz-Baldes and Lars Koekenbier

