	\draw[black, thick] (2.5,0.5) .. controls (3,0.5) and (4,0.3) .. (4,0);
    \end{tikzpicture},\end{center}
    there is exactly one additional Bell pair shared across the bond $l$, hence the entanglement entropy increases by $1$.
    \item $S_{l+1}(\ket{\pi(C_{l-1}})) = S_{l}(\ket{\pi(C_{l-1})}) - 1$. Here, there exists a qubit $a$, $1<a<l$, that shares a Bell pair with qubit qubit $l+1$. When performing the SWAP,
    \begin{center}\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.67]
    \foreach \k in {0,1,3,4} {\filldraw[black] (\k,0) circle (3pt);}
    \draw[-{latex}, black, line width=1.5pt] (1.5,0) -- (2.5,0);
	\draw[black, thick] (-0.5,0.6) .. controls (-0.2,0.4) and (0,0.3) .. (0,0);
	\draw[black, thick] (-0.5,0.4) .. controls (0,0.35) and (1,0.3) .. (1,0);
	\draw[black, thick] (2.5,0.4) .. controls (2.8,0.35) and (3,0.3) .. (3,0);
	\draw[black, thick] (2.5,0.6) .. controls (3,0.55) and (4,0.3) .. (4,0);
