Finally, the refined output is combined with the original input via a learnable residual connection:
\begin{equation}
F_{\text{GAST\_out}} = \alpha \cdot F_{\text{enhanced}} + F_{\text{latent}},
\end{equation}
where \( \alpha \in \mathbb{R} \) is a learnable scalar initialized to 1.0, and \( F_{\text{latent}} \) denotes the original input to the GAST module. This design facilitates gradient flow and provides additional modeling capacity for feature enhancement.

