\paragraph{Summary and perspective}
We have developed a sign-problem-free lattice nuclear force, enabling unbiased QMC simulations across the nuclear chart. 
This interaction reasonably reproduces experimental binding energies from $^4$He to $^{132}$Sn and nuclear matter saturation with statistical errors of around $1$ MeV at a feasible computational cost. 
The approach can be directly extended to investigate excited-state spectra~\cite{PRL106-192501}, density correlations~\cite{PRL119-222505}, and finite-temperature nuclear properties~\cite{PRL125-192502} using advanced lattice QMC algorithms.
Future refinements will incorporate more nuclei and additional nuclear observables to further constrain the interaction.
Moreover, this interaction provides an robust non-perturbative foundation for \textit{ab initio} calculations with high-fidelity nuclear chiral forces.
The missing physics in our model can be incorporated order-by-order perturbatively~\cite{PRL128-242501, Nature630-59}.
Finally, this work provides a scalable and systematically improvable computational paradigm that bridges \textit{ab initio} calculations and phenomenological models.


