Fig.~\ref{fig:Oxygen} presents binding energies per nucleon across the oxygen isotopic chain for both even-$A$ and odd-$A$ nuclei. 
The inset displays corresponding average phases. 
Calculations for odd nucleon numbers introduce a mild sign oscillation due to slight time-reversal symmetry breaking, yet yield statistical uncertainties comparable to even-$A$ nuclei, indicating no significant efficiency degradation. 
The computed energies reproduce odd-even staggering with slightly overestimated pairing gaps. 
Discrepancies at large neutron numbers may indicate missing interaction components (e.g., tensor forces).

