The finite element mesh comprised 14,443  eight-node biquadratic displacement, bilinear temperature elements (Abaqus type CPE8T). The mesh was refined in the region where cracking was anticipated, ensuring that the smallest element size was maintained at one-fifth of the characteristic length \(\ell\). The monolithic scheme was employed to solve the coupled deformation-fracture problem, while a multi-pass staggered scheme is adopted to handle the coupling with the fluid equation. 100 increments are used, each spanning 20 seconds.


