\subsection{Reflection}

Stock price forecasting is a challenging task that has evolved from using traditional statistical methods, such as ARIMA and GARCH, to more advanced machine learning and deep learning methods. Although machine learning methods improved the handling of non-linear data, as seen in SVR, KNN, and Random Forest, they have drawbacks in computational efficiency and handling high-dimensional data, such as time series. These drawbacks can be overcome by using Deep Learning methods such as LSTM, \(\alpha\)-RNNs, Graph Neural Networks (GNNs), and Federated Learning with LLMs. 
LSTM networks above all have emerged to be a leading solution by effectively capturing short and long-term dependencies in financial time series data while being computationally efficient. 


