\section{Contamination}
\label{sec:contamination}

Since the securities reports included in EDINET-Bench are publicly available on the Internet, there is a potential for contamination. As a simple check, we conduct company name prediction and year-wise performance analysis.

\paragraph{Company name prediction}
To confirm whether the LLM already knew the content of the securities reports used in the evaluation dataset, we measure the performance of a task where the model is given tabular data (BS, CF, PL, Summary) from the test split of the accounting fraud detection dataset and asked to predict the company names. The prompt is shown in Figure~\ref{prompt:company_name}.
For evaluation, we allowed minor company name variations such as including or omitting ``Kabushiki Kaisha'' by relying on the LLM-as-a-judge approach.
For all models, the accuracy is below 0.05, indicating the difficulty for models to associate tabular data with company names.
