The statement follows from the facts that the Jacobian isomorphism $\Phi_{\rm mir}^{u=0, y=0}$ is a ring isomorphism, and that $(\sum_{j=1}^{r} \frac{\deg(q_{j})}{2}q_{j}\frac{\partial}{\partial q_{j}}+ \mu_{A} )$ satisfies the Leibniz rule. 
